      "content": "Neighborhood stability is often tied to the underlying socioeconomic makeup of the area. Data points reflecting the concentration of certain demographics or the historical economic trends of a specific zip code can be very telling. Areas with consistent, established populations and lower rates of recent turnover tend to show more predictable repayment patterns. You should look closely at metrics that indicate long-term community investment rather than transient population shifts.",
